Z||000003||LT1 Chop Top||10-16-2001||06:58 PM||||Thanks for the compliments all around guys!<P>The Chop Top is one heck of a car.  I fell in love with it the first time I saw it on Archie's web site.  It is so much fun to drive, even though there isn't a place I can put it into 5th gear legally!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I JUST got it back from having it buffed and the exhaust redone (less restrictive).  IT looks beautiful and sounds MEANER!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <P>The amount of attention this car gets at shows (anywhere really) is always cool.  We have some extremely sharp Fieros in our local club, including a 88 Yellow t-top Formula, and my 88 GT which has received 1st place seven times out of eight showings (got 2nd to a sweet low mile 85 GT racer), and the Chop Top gets 90% of the attention at shows.<P>Getting looks, pissing off Pony cars, and Type "R's" is certainly fun and cool, but I enjoy it most when I am all alone in the twisties of the Texas Hill Country w/ the sunroof off.  Again thanks for the compliments, and as always, all credit goes to Archie.......<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/c12.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000004||Archie||10-16-2001||08:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B> and as always, all credit goes to Archie.......<BR>  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope, you're wrong on that one. If I'd have kept the car I would have driven it year 'round in rain snow whatever, & I'd have ragged on it all the time. <P>I build them to drive 'em. You've taken a lot better care of the car than I would have. <P>So all the credit is your's.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tryxalon||10-16-2001||08:18 PM||||Whoever is to blame - <P>It is a car to make every carnut drool. <P>It is a car to make one envious. <P>Very nice car!!  <P>||||reg||1
